    "assumptions": [
      "Asset is BTCUSDT because the claim says Bitcoin; timeframe 1d from the parenthetical about chart time period and page timeframe.",
      "Direction is long: Saturday sell is an exit to flat to avoid Sunday weakness and Wednesday buy-back is a re-entry; a short-sale reading is possible but long-flat avoidance is the most natural spot reading.",
      "Calendar timing: buy on Wednesday means signal on Tuesday's close filling Wednesday's open; sell on Saturday means signal on Friday's close filling Saturday's open, because rules are evaluated on bar closes and fill at the next open.",
      "Exit uses a single day_of_week gt 3.5 to mean Friday-close signal; Saturday/Sunday signals are redundant when flat and a single condition is needed because exits trigger on ANY.",
      "'kinda going up' interpreted as close above SMA(50) as a concrete uptrend filter; alternatives in free_parameters.",
      "No stop, target, trailing stop or max hold stated; the Friday-close condition provides the required exit."
    ],
